ally because i i'm not that fluent  in spanish but uh congressman jimenez i  know had a discussion with the family  that  uh made the journey from haiti and in  talking to the agents you find out that  they're coming from all over the world  china especially and china being the big  fish because they'll actually pay 35 000  to be brought into the country well but  one of the most staggering statistics i  heard yesterday was the idea that  they're paying on the average of four  thousand dollars uh  to have these coyotes push them into the  country now think about that last some  not just last month  they've caught a hundred thousand that's  400 million dollars  so there's a and that and think of the  people we didn't catch so there's a huge  financial incentive for this to occur as  well let's take a look at some of the  stats the southern border migrating  migration encounters we have a full  screen 100 441 came in february of 2021.  that's stunning that's up 28 from  january up 174  from february 2020 the highest since  june of 2019.  so this is stunning congressman uh  congresswoman  harrell when you look at this situation  where is this heading where are we going  to be in three weeks where we're going  to be in a month  oh it's certainly this is a crisis at  the border and it really didn't have to  be this way and in fact  one of our colleagues i think said it  best yesterday uh congressman mike  mccloud said  you know this administration could have  done nothing and it would have been  better than it is right  now because we know the policies of  president trump are working with the  remain in mexico  right now we're hoping that they keep  the title 42 in place  that is actually what's helping that's  the public health order  that allows border patrol agents to  process on the border  those that are coming here illegally  from mexico or canada and then expel  them back to  mexico or canada that is uh one of the  tools that is working the board patrol  told us yesterday that has been a  godsend they hope that that title 42  stays in place and we've actually  introduced legislation doing just that  so we're hoping that we can get some  legs under that piece of legislation and  get it through so that we can keep that  available for our board patrol agents  and for the country  unaccompanied miners you have 9457 in  february  so congressman rose when they turn  around and say this is all  trump's fault it was broken policies  broken border we inherited what's your  reaction  well i think that's ridiculous i think  that president biden's  message that he sent that the border  would be open and that  these individuals should come is  encouraging them to come and putting  those people in harm's way as they make  the perilous journey north  and so i think it's ridiculous to lay  this at the feet of  of president trump because clearly this  is biden's  crisis it's biden's scandal and he won't  even admit it and he will not let the  border patrol talk about it but yet the  stress is overwhelming  uh congress people have to leave it  there harold rose  and joyce thanks for making the journey  giving us your personal uh  account of what you saw rather than  reports and what you read  thank you so much thank you thank you  thank you you got it
 

